BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Record Store Day Black Friday @ the Squatch Den
DTSTART:20261127T130000Z
DTEND:20261128T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261126T185810Z
UID:9553535a4902e225e756a765dcb4bacbd45089cf@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Event by The Squatch Den Records\n3300 Chambers Rd\nHorseheads
 \, NY\nPublic\nRecord Store Day Black Friday is approaching fast and the l
 ist was just made live!\nBe sure to check out 'The List' and fill out our 
 Google Form (in the comment section here and on our main page) to help us 
 bring you the best experience possible.\nOur doors will open at 8AM on 11/
 27\, but people will start lining up as early as the night before. There a
 re rules put in place by RSD that ALL participating stores must follow to 
 be able to continue participating in future events. To put it as bluntly a
 s possible\, we will not bend the rules to appease a single person as this
  can damage our abilities to participate in Record Store Day.\nRSD Rules:
 \n- First come\, first served\n- No holds\, preorders\, or any sort of pre
 -purchase is available.\n- All titles are one copy per person per title (i
 f there is a red version and a yellow version\, you can order one of each)
 .\n- No line cutting\, budging\, holding\, etc.\n- Have a great time!\nMor
 e details will be added to our page\, this event page\, as well as our gro
 up\, THE VINYL DISPENSARY.\nWe look forward to sharing this amazing day wi
 th all of you!\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/
 event/78518455/20261127080000
GEO:42.160134;-76.873177
LOCATION:Arnot Mall\, 3300 Chambers Road\, Horseheads\, New York\, 14845\,
  United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78518455/20261127080000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:70th Annual Downtown Elmira Holiday Parade
DTSTART:20261127T150000Z
DTEND:20261128T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261126T185810Z
UID:000177e468f41c4f67df32456771498373e7a6d3@corning-events
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Holidays,Community,Family Fun,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:Event by Elmira Downtown Development\, Inc\nDowntown Elmira\nP
 ublic\n70th Annual Downtown Elmira Holiday Parade\nFriday\, November 27 
 • 10:00 AM • Downtown Elmira\nFREE Community Event\, Sponsored by Comm
 unity Bank\, N.A.\nKick off the holiday season in the heart of downtown El
 mira at the 70th Annual Downtown Elmira Holiday Parade! This beloved tradi
 tion brings together families\, local businesses\, performers\, and commun
 ity groups for a magical morning full of festive fun.\nWhat to Expect:\n
 • Festive Floats from local organizations\, businesses and emergency res
 ponse vehicles!\n• Marching Band & Local Performers bringing lively holi
 day music and entertainment\n• Special Appearance by Santa Claus and hun
 dreds of costumed characters spreading cheer to kids and families\n• Com
 munity Spirit Everywhere as neighbors line the streets to celebrate the se
 ason together\nParade Route:\nThe parade steps off from Water Street near 
 Elmira Tea & Coffee House and concludes at Wisner Park. Bundle up\, grab y
 our spot\, and enjoy the sights and sounds of the season!\nFor 70 years th
 e Elmira Holiday Parade has been a tradition that families have not only l
 oved to see\, but to participate in!\nCome to our costume fittings if you 
 are interested in being in the parade this year!\nVisit www.elmiradowntown
 .com for details\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzp
 j/event/78507661/20261127100000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507661/20261127100000
END:VEVENT
